[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3797329142","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115361#issuecomment-3797329142","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115361","id":3797329142,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7iVqT2","user":{"login":"Tom3s","id":55595037,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NTk1MDM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55595037?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tom3s","html_url":"https://github.com/Tom3s","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tom3s/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tom3s/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tom3s/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tom3s/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tom3s/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tom3s/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tom3s/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tom3s/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tom3s/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-25T22:22:01Z","updated_at":"2026-01-25T22:22:18Z","body":"After further investigation, it makes sense for the model to show the color presented in the video as described by another user:\n\nwell 0.0 is *the left edge*, not *the center of the leftmost pixel*. so with repeat enabled, it'll blend the 2 pixels bordering the left edge: the leftmost and rightmost pixel. same thing with 1.0 but with the right edge.  \n(assuming filtering is not set to \"nearest neighbor\", in which it would pick one of the edge's neighboring pixels at random instead of blending them)\n\nso tldr: disable repeat if you dont want it to... repeat.\n\nHowever there were 2 things that confused me:\n\n1. I used a gradient with only two colors, so from the left edge to the right edge the interpolation at 0.5 was the same as from the right to the left (which works as expected)\n\n2. The preview inside the shader hraph showed the color correctly. But given the response of the other user I believe the preview is showing an incorrect color, rather the mesh itself","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3797329142/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3804415022","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115361#issuecomment-3804415022","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115361","id":3804415022,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7iwsQu","user":{"login":"celyk","id":50609684,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNjA5Njg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50609684?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk","html_url":"https://github.com/celyk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-27T10:39:06Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T10:39:06Z","body":"It looks like the texture in the preview is clamped by mistake. Could it be using a different sampler with repeat disabled?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin"